        "Note": "DomainName must follow the region: us-east-1 uses ec2.internal, every other region <region>.compute.internal. This is the rule AWS applies when no option set is created at all.\n\nA hardcoded ec2.internal outside us-east-1 looks harmless because nothing fails - but every instance then carries a search domain and a hostname that do not resolve. Agents asking for their own FQDN get NXDOMAIN on a timer, which is pure noise in the DNS query log and forces a whitelist entry that only exists to silence it. Option sets are immutable: changing this replaces the resource and re-associates the VPC. Running instances keep their resolv.conf until the DHCP lease renews or they reboot."
